# API Contract (v2) — build to these shapes

This contract is shared with the iOS client (`lifesight-ios`, `LifesightAPI.swift`).
Changing a shape here is a cross-repo breaking change — flag it (see the escalation
protocol in `00-core.mdc`) instead of changing it unilaterally.

v2 knowingly extends the prior frozen contract with additive optional
`visual_panel` and `research` fields and expanded mode strings. See
`CONTEXT.md`, `AGENTS.md`, and
`docs/V2_BRAINSTORM_MAIL_CALENDAR_CONTRACT.md`.

**Runtime note:** until slice 1 lands, live `/modes` may still return only
`fitness`/`diet`/`author`. The shapes below are the **approved target contract**.

## POST /chat
Request:
```json
{
  "transcript": "how many sets left?",
  "mode": "fitness",
  "conversation_id": "abc123"
}
```
`mode` for active clients is one of
`"fitness" | "diet" | "author" | "brainstorm" | "mail_calendar"`.
(`jarvis` may remain registered server-side for legacy/debug routing but is
hidden from `GET /modes` and the iOS UI; never silently reused for
`mail_calendar`. `health` is retired.)
`conversation_id` is `null` on the first message of a session.

Response:
```json
{
  "reply": "You're on set 3 of bench press.",
  "mode": "fitness",
  "conversation_id": "abc123",
  "pending_action": null,
  "visual_panel": {
    "type": "workout_sets",
    "data": {}
  },
  "research": null,
  "client_actions": []
}
```
`conversation_id` is server-generated if the request's was `null`.
`pending_action` is `null` unless something irreversible needs confirmation.
`pending_action.description` is READ ALOUD — a natural spoken sentence.
`visual_panel` is optional/nullable (`{type, data} | null`).
`research` is optional/nullable and **separate from** `visual_panel`.
`client_actions` is always an array (never null). V1 items are
`{ "type": "navigate", "target": "<allowlist>" }` only. Ordinary turns return
`[]`. Navigation is client-local — **not** Confirm Gate. Spoken field remains
`reply` (not `assistant_text`). Older clients that ignore unknown fields remain
compatible.

### `client_actions` (V1 — navigate only)
Allowlisted `target` values (closed set):
`home` | `fitness` | `diet` | `author` | `brainstorm` | `mail_calendar` | `settings`

Never emit `jarvis` or `health`. Deterministic whole-utterance commands
(`open` / `go to` / `take me to` / …) are handled before mode Claude.

Example navigate turn:
```json
{
  "reply": "Opening Fitness.",
  "mode": "diet",
  "conversation_id": "abc123",
  "pending_action": null,
  "visual_panel": null,
  "research": null,
  "client_actions": [{ "type": "navigate", "target": "fitness" }]
}
```

### `research` (Brainstorm; usually null elsewhere)
```json
{
  "status": "completed",
  "query": "…",
  "summary": "…",
  "uncertainty": "…",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "…",
      "url": "https://…",
      "publisher": "…",
      "retrieved_at": "2026-08-04T20:00:00Z"
    }
  ],
  "fact_check": {
    "claim": "…",
    "verdict": "supported",
    "confidence": 0.72
  }
}
```
- `status`: `"not_requested" | "completed" | "failed" | "unavailable"`
  (no `running` until streaming research exists).
- Public sources: `title`, `url`, `publisher`, `retrieved_at` — **no** `snippet`
  in the initial iOS contract.
- `fact_check` only when `status == "completed"` and a real web-search ran.
- `verdict`: `"supported" | "partially_supported" | "not_supported" | "inconclusive"`.
- First research provider: Anthropic native web search behind a
  `ResearchProvider` abstraction (Tavily/Brave later).

## POST /confirm
Request: `{ "action_id": "act_789", "approved": true }`
Response: `{ "result": "Saved: …" }`

`approved: false` discards the pending action entirely and must not execute anything.

## GET /modes
Response (exact order — do not alphabetically sort):
`{ "modes": ["fitness", "diet", "author", "brainstorm", "mail_calendar"] }`

(`jarvis` is not advertised; `health` is retired. String array is fine for v1;
structured mode-config may come later.)

## GET /health
Response: `{ "status": "ok" }`

## POST /voice/speech
Server-side TTS only (ElevenLabs). iOS must not embed ElevenLabs API keys.

Request: `{ "text": "Opening Author." }` with `Authorization: Bearer <access JWT>`.
Response: `audio/mpeg` (streamed). Env: `ELEVENLABS_API_KEY`, `ELEVENLABS_VOICE_ID`
(optional `ELEVENLABS_MODEL_ID`, default `eleven_flash_v2_5`).

## GET /me
Response: `{ "user_id": "<uuid>" }` — resolved identity for the current auth token.

## Auth (v2)
Login options: email/password, magic link, Sign in with Apple — all via backend
proxies so iOS does not embed Supabase secrets:
- `POST /auth/signup` `{email, password}`
- `POST /auth/login` `{email, password}`
- `POST /auth/magic-link` `{email}`
- `POST /auth/apple` `{id_token, nonce?}`

Every authenticated request resolves identity via
`Authorization: Bearer <token>` through `Depends(get_current_user_id)` in
`shared/auth.py`.
- `AUTH_MODE=dev` (default): any Bearer token, or none at all, resolves to a fixed
  dev UUID.
- `AUTH_MODE=real`: verifies the Supabase JWT signature, audience, and expiry.
  Requires `SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET`.
- Never decode tokens outside `shared/auth.py`.
- The iOS client must never assert its own `user_id` in a request body.

## POST /devices, GET /devices, DELETE /devices/{device_id}
Unchanged from v1 device registration shapes.

## Confirm Gate scope (v2)
Irreversible/destructive only: e.g. `save_food_entry`, `delete_scene`, and
Mail & Calendar send / delete / archive / event create-update-delete /
attendee invite / invitation response. Ordinary workout set logs, reversible
scene edits, Brainstorm research, and mail/calendar read-search-draft /
free-busy do **not** create `pending_action`.

## Domain endpoints (summary)
- Fitness: `POST /workouts/session/start`, `POST /workouts/voice-log`,
  `GET /workouts/session/{id}/state`
- Diet: `POST /food/photo|barcode|voice` (drafts), `POST /food/entries` (stages
  Confirm Gate pending action)
- Author: manuscript/chapter/scene CRUD under `/manuscripts/...`,
  `POST /author/brainstorm-session` (rename from `/author/brainstorm` before
  global Brainstorm mode ships)
- Wearables: `POST /wearables/connect`, `POST /wearables/terra/webhook`
- Mail & Calendar: Google-first under `mail_calendar` packages (OAuth + tools
  in later slices; not via legacy Jarvis modules)

## Conversation memory
`conversation_id` ties multi-turn exchanges together. History is Postgres-backed.
The app sends `null` to start fresh (e.g. switching modes) and echoes back
whatever id the server returns on every subsequent message.
